     "tests_dust_pop": "that popping a dust position is economically harmless in every state — it proves the rule (strictly below the name's venue min notional ⇒ popped before the reshape; the clamp keeps a flatten row at 0.0; no order-bearing row) on synthetic books and on ONE recorded anchor (2026-09-25 08Z), not across the ledger. Two blind spots, each real: (a) the floor is the executor's cached min_notional — a venue floor that changed since the cache was written is not seen here; (b) a dust residual whose VALUE later grows above the floor (a large price move while held) returns to the clamp at that anchor, and nothing here tests that transition on real data",
+    "tests_quantity_unknowns": "that every unknown-read-as-zero on the money path is gone — it proves the SEVEN sites of the R25-01 triage (position_break bucket gross, reconcile _qty_of, the external dust floor, the anchor_loop floor map, child-fill sums, userTrades rows, the watchdog NAV flow) refuse an absent quantity, each against the pre-fix module on the same input. The census that found them is a static LOWER BOUND (its detector does not follow a value through a local variable), and the 20 low sites are listed for the next package, not fixed here",
     "tests_orphan_position": "that a withheld-and-held name will actually be REDUCED at the venue — it proves the target survives the clamp so plan() emits a row, not that the order fills; a venue that refuses reduce orders too would still strand the position",
     "tests_frontier_staleness": "that the frontier marker the upstream publishes is CORRECT — it proves we consume it and that a frozen frontier is no longer a pass. If the producer published a wrong newest_scored_anchor this consumer would believe it. ★ SINCE 2026-09-13 (ALM-03) IT PINS A RETIRED EVALUATOR: ops/check_factor_health.py is no longer called by the anchor (step 9 runs ops/check_rank_monitor_input.py) and its ssh source has had no producer since 2026-08-06, so a green here says nothing about what the anchor monitors now — that is tests_rank_monitor_input",
     "tests_head_liveness": "that a head which passes the liveness test is USEFUL — it proves a collapsed head is caught and that the verdict is scale-free, not that a live head carries signal. IC is what says that, and no liveness test can",
